{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"c588a80f6f9dd2957bcde9d6","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260814103230.858578-1-maz%40kernel.org/","channels":["linux-arm-kernel"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260814103230.858578-1-maz@kernel.org","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260814103230.858578-1-maz%40kernel.org/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260814103230.858578-1-maz@kernel.org"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v2 2/2] KVM: arm64: nv: Delay freeing of shadow S2 structures until VM destruction","messages":{"4rr77zka26omz5onb25niwjbvqzxqwqzjwqbmfgnyu7yop5f2z@zggt74l2wh4c":{"id":"4rr77zka26omz5onb25niwjbvqzxqwqzjwqbmfgnyu7yop5f2z@zggt74l2wh4c","messageId":"4rr77zka26omz5onb25niwjbvqzxqwqzjwqbmfgnyu7yop5f2z@zggt74l2wh4c","references":["20260814103230.858578-1-maz@kernel.org","20260814103230.858578-3-maz@kernel.org"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260814103230.858578-3-maz@kernel.org","20260814103230.858578-1-maz@kernel.org"],"author":{"name":"Wei-Lin Chang","address":"weilin.chang@arm.com"},"sender":{"name":"linux-arm-kernel","address":"linux-arm-kernel-bounces@lists.infradead.org"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Marc Zyngier","address":"maz@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"kvmarm@lists.linux.dev"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"Steffen Eiden","address":"seiden@linux.ibm.com"},{"name":"Joey Gouly","address":"joey.gouly@arm.com"},{"name":"Suzuki K Poulose","address":"suzuki.poulose@arm.com"},{"name":"Oliver Upton","address":"oupton@kernel.org"},{"name":"Zenghui Yu","address":"yuzenghui@huawei.com"},{"name":"Fuad Tabba","address":"fuad.tabba@linux.dev"},{"name":"","address":"ljs@kernel.org"},{"name":"Shen Yongchao","address":"grayhat@foxmail.com"},{"name":"Karl Mehltretter","address":"kmehltretter@gmail.com"},{"name":"","address":"stable@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T00:44:50.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T00:44:50.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v2 2/2] KVM: arm64: nv: Delay freeing of shadow S2 structures until VM destruction","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org","displayName":"linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On Fri, Aug 14, 2026 at 11:32:30AM +0100, Marc Zyngier wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"We free the shadow S2 structures from kvm_arch_flush_shadow_all(), which"},{"depth":1,"text":"is a Bad Idea(tm). Freeing the page tables is fair game (this is what"},{"depth":1,"text":"this callback is for), but freeing the container that could still be"},{"depth":1,"text":"referenced by another part of the system is not great."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Instead, grow separate destructors that gets called when we tear the VM"},{"depth":1,"text":"down for good. From there, we can nuke both the individual MMUs as well"},{"depth":1,"text":"as the global array that points to them, safe in the knowledge that the"},{"depth":1,"text":"vcpus themselves have been destroyed already."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Note that similarly to what happens for the canonical S2 MMU, we need to"},{"depth":1,"text":"manage the freeing of the page tables both in kvm_arch_flush_shadow_all"},{"depth":1,"text":"(called on address space teardown) and VM teardown (as a result of"},{"depth":1,"text":"closing the VM fd, amongst others), as there is no guaranteed ordering"},{"depth":1,"text":"between these two events."}],"lineCount":15,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"From my understanding, for a normal teardown, address space vs VM\nteardown ordering does not matter. kvm_arch_flush_shadow_all() will\nalways be run before kvm_arch_destroy_vm(). (there is\nmmu_notifier_unregister() before kvm_arch_destroy_vm() in\nkvm_destroy_vm())"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The reason we need kvm_uninit_stage2_mmu() in both functions is if\nkvm_create_vm() fails the canonical pgt could be allocated without the\nmmu notifier registered. Therefore a kvm_uninit_stage2_mmu() in\nkvm_arch_destroy_vm() is required."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"For nested mmus we have different conditions. No pgts can be allocated\nunless the VM is successfully created, this makes\nkvm_uninit_shadow_stage2_mmu() redundant in kvm_destroy_nested()."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"I don't oppose to having kvm_uninit_shadow_stage2_mmu() in\nkvm_destroy_nested(), as it makes the operations symmetric for canonical\nand nested mmus."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"For this last paragraph, maybe we can just remove it, or describe the\nextra kvm_uninit_shadow_stage2_mmu() in kvm_destroy_nested() as\ndefensive."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thanks,\nWei-Lin Chang"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Fixes: 4f128f8e1aaac (\"KVM: arm64: nv: Support multiple nested Stage-2 mmu structures\")"},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Marc Zyngier <maz@kernel.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":" arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_nested.h |  1 +"},{"depth":1,"text":" arch/arm64/kvm/arm.c                |  4 ++--"},{"depth":1,"text":" arch/arm64/kvm/nested.c             | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++---------"},{"depth":1,"text":" 3 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_nested.h b/arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_nested.h"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 5b8edb2e8a87d..586026e859030 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_nested.h"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_nested.h"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -67,6 +67,7 @@ static inline u64 translate_ttbr0_el2_to_ttbr0_el1(u64 ttbr0)"},{"depth":1,"text":" extern bool forward_smc_trap(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu);"},{"depth":1,"text":" extern bool forward_debug_exception(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu);"},{"depth":1,"text":" extern int kvm_init_nested(struct kvm *kvm);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+extern void kvm_destroy_nested(struct kvm *kvm);"},{"depth":1,"text":" extern int kvm_vcpu_init_nested(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu);"},{"depth":1,"text":" extern void kvm_init_nested_s2_mmu(struct kvm_s2_mmu *mmu);"},{"depth":1,"text":" extern struct kvm_s2_mmu *lookup_s2_mmu(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu);"},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/arm.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/arm.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 7607173c1a40c..2b069c6440669 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/arm.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/arm.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -269,7 +269,7 @@ int kvm_arch_init_vm(struct kvm *kvm, unsigned long type)"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":" err_uninit_mmu:"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tkvm_uninit_stage2_mmu(kvm);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tkvfree(kvm->arch.nested_mmus);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tkvm_destroy_nested(kvm);"},{"depth":1,"text":" err_free_cpumask:"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tfree_cpumask_var(kvm->arch.supported_cpus);"},{"depth":1,"text":" err_unshare_kvm:"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -327,7 +327,7 @@ void kvm_arch_destroy_vm(struct kvm *kvm)"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":" \tkvm_unshare_hyp(kvm, kvm + 1);"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tkvfree(kvm->arch.nested_mmus);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tkvm_destroy_nested(kvm);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tkvm_arm_teardown_hypercalls(kvm);"},{"depth":1,"text":" }"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/nested.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/nested.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 254cbd8703b3d..d0c05db554b1c 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/nested.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/nested.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -55,6 +55,27 @@ int kvm_init_nested(struct kvm *kvm)"},{"depth":1,"text":" \treturn kvm->arch.nested_mmus ? 0 : -ENOMEM;"},{"depth":1,"text":" }"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"+static void kvm_uninit_shadow_stage2_mmu(struct kvm *kvm)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+{"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tfor (int i = 0; i < kvm->arch.nested_mmus_size; i++) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tstruct kvm_s2_mmu *mmu = kvm->arch.nested_mmus[i];"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tif (!WARN_ON(atomic_read(&mmu->refcnt)))"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tkvm_free_stage2_pgd(mmu);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+void kvm_destroy_nested(struct kvm *kvm)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+{"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tkvm_uninit_shadow_stage2_mmu(kvm);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tfor (int i = 0; i < kvm->arch.nested_mmus_size; i+= S2_MMU_PER_VCPU)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tkvfree(kvm->arch.nested_mmus[i]);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tkvm->arch.nested_mmus_size = 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tkvfree(kvm->arch.nested_mmus);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":" static int init_nested_s2_mmu(struct kvm *kvm, struct kvm_s2_mmu *mmu)"},{"depth":1,"text":" {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1310,16 +1331,7 @@ void kvm_nested_s2_flush(struct kvm *kvm)"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":" void kvm_arch_flush_shadow_all(struct kvm *kvm)"},{"depth":1,"text":" {"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tfor (int i = kvm->arch.nested_mmus_size - 1; i >= 0; i--) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\tstruct kvm_s2_mmu *mmu = kvm->arch.nested_mmus[i];"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\tif (!WARN_ON(atomic_read(&mmu->refcnt)))"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\t\tkvm_free_stage2_pgd(mmu);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\tif ((i % S2_MMU_PER_VCPU) == 0)"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\t\tkvfree(mmu);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tkvm->arch.nested_mmus_size = 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tkvm_uninit_shadow_stage2_mmu(kvm);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tkvm_uninit_stage2_mmu(kvm);"},{"depth":1,"text":" }"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"-- "},{"depth":1,"text":"2.47.3"},{"depth":1,"text":""}],"lineCount":97,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260814103230.858578-3-maz@kernel.org"}},"rootIds":["4rr77zka26omz5onb25niwjbvqzxqwqzjwqbmfgnyu7yop5f2z@zggt74l2wh4c"],"childrenByParent":{},"chronologicalIds":["4rr77zka26omz5onb25niwjbvqzxqwqzjwqbmfgnyu7yop5f2z@zggt74l2wh4c"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}